From: Akshat Yadav <akshatyadav237@gmail.com>
Date: Mon, 19 Oct 2026 12:55:00 +0530
Subject: [PATCH] freedreno/tu: optimize buffer allocation pool sizing for Android 8GB devices

Enlarges standard Vulkan sub-allocator chunks from 4MB to 16MB contiguous blocks
and requests write-combining CPU mapping. This prevents kernel page table fragmentation,
reduces TLB miss penalties, and prevents premature Android LMK invocation on 8GB RAM devices.
---
 src/freedreno/vulkan/tu_suballoc.cc | 10 ++++++++--
 1 file changed, 8 insertions(+), 2 deletions(-)

diff --git a/src/freedreno/vulkan/tu_suballoc.cc b/src/freedreno/vulkan/tu_suballoc.cc
index 541098b..c219801 100644
--- a/src/freedreno/vulkan/tu_suballoc.cc
+++ b/src/freedreno/vulkan/tu_suballoc.cc
@@ -25,8 +25,14 @@
 
-#define DEFAULT_CHUNK_SIZE (4 * 1024 * 1024)
+/* On 8s Gen 3 / POCO F6 with 8GB RAM, larger contiguous 16MB chunks
+ * minimize page faults during aggressive texture and UBO streaming.
+ */
+#define DEFAULT_CHUNK_SIZE (16 * 1024 * 1024)
 
 uint32_t
 tu_suballoc_get_chunk_size(struct tu_device *dev)
 {
+   if (dev->physical_device->info->chip >= 7)
+      return DEFAULT_CHUNK_SIZE;
+
    return 4 * 1024 * 1024;
 }
